K1 and K2.
- §2: add a mapping note (details in references/research/korea/statistics.md; the audience contract does not change):
  - approved national statistics with an approval number: official_statistics;
  - surveys by public research institutes and independent pollsters with a stated n: research_paper;
  - app-panel, traffic and ad-research vendors: market_report.
- §3: modelled traffic demographics of a community are at most D for share kinds.
- §4, new downgrade rows:
  - researcher note: one grade lower; paraphrase in shared outputs;
  - review-event incentive: at most D;
  - virtual person: E;
  - polarity uncertain: cannot support satisfaction or counter-search outcomes.
  The inline Korean and English marker lists are replaced by principles:
  - any wording of a disclosure reveals the relationship, including KFTC's 'unclear' labels;
  - no disclosure in the text is not proof of an organic post;
  - 내돈내산 and 광고 아님 carry no weight.
  Then a pointer to markers.json and references/research/korea/promotion.md.
- §5:
  - channel families gain commerce_reviews;
  - the Statistics Korea example becomes 국가데이터처 (named 통계청 until 2025-10-01; aliases in korea-statistics.json);
  - posts signed ㅇㅇ count by thread.
- §6: counts of people who chose to complain or report (1372 counselling, KFTC monitoring) are never denominators.
- §10: add platform discontinuities (see the platform map), and judge a promotion disclosure against the rule valid at published_at (2020-09-01, 2024-12-01, 2026-06-01).
- The credit stays.

K1.
- Query expansion: a pointer to references/research/korea/query-craft.md (portal operators, the lexicon, 초성체, 야민정음, slang).
- Capture record adds:
  - promotion check (where it was found, or text only, or incentive, or virtual person);
  - polarity (clear or uncertain);
  - speech cues (hearsay ending, register shift);
  - store and storefront, and review window;
  - access basis (reader or researcher note).
- 'What not to infer' adds:
  - register or address terms (존댓말, 반말, 형, 언니, 이모, 님) are not age or gender;
  - 내돈내산 is not proof of independence, and a missing disclosure is not proof of an organic post;
  - a star average where review events run is not satisfaction;
  - a community's gender or age mix from panels or wikis is not a share;
  - a complaint-line or regulator count is not a prevalence.

K0 and K2.
- access_basis adds researcher_note (a person read a public page in their own browser; paraphrase in shared outputs; graded one step lower).
- access_method adds researcher.
- The access block drops engine_version; rung is 'R0 to R3'; presentation drops browser_equivalent_tls; stop_class adds terms_restricted.
- Optional source fields:
  - incentive_flags, virtual_person_flags;
  - promo_check (text_only | text_and_images);
  - stat_card {publisher, title, approval_no, table_id, reference_period, frame, n, method, sampling_error, unit, value_as_printed, url, retrieved_at, licence};
  - retention_until;
  - terms {status, checked_by_user}.
- platform_family values gain commerce_reviews.
- Planned validator check: a statistical source that supports a size claim needs stat_card.frame and reference_period.

K1. English with Korean names.
1. What the map is: planning knowledge. Reader policy lives in routes.json. Audience figures are leads, never shares (source-grading.md section 6). checked_at is 2026-09-29, from search summaries; verified_at stays null until a live check (ux_research.py robots plus a human read of the terms). Platform names are descriptive; no affiliation.
2. One table row per JSON id, in the same order (enforced by a test). Columns: id, 채널, family, who posts (lead; confidence), voice bias, public scope, legitimate route, expected stops, terms status.
3. Under-covered audiences:
   - people in their 50s and 60s, in Band and KakaoTalk (KPF 2024: 40.6% of people in their 50s use Band);
   - students, in Everytime;
   - closed cafes.
   Use surveys or interviews for these groups.
4. Store and review skews: App Store against Google Play (Gallup 2025); delivery-app review events (KCA 2024); the own-brand staff-review case (KFTC 2024-284).
5. Discontinuities:
   - Naver Place stars: removed 2021-10, restored 2026-04-06, averages public from 2026-07-09;
   - KakaoTalk redesign, 2025-09-23;
   - Kakao Map web overhaul, 2025-03;
   - DC Inside sale, 2026-03;
   - Daum operator change, 2025-12-01, renamed 2026-07-27;
   - Naver Search API moved to API HUB: new keys stopped 2026-07-31; legacy keys end 2027-06-30.
6. How to update a row: robots check, human read of the terms with URL and date, bump checked_at. Never add undocumented endpoints or search pages.
7. Sources: a keyed URL list identical to the JSON's URLs (a test checks it).
8. Done when / Failure modes (short).

K1 and K2. Uses import _paths.
- korea-platforms.json:
  - required fields and enums;
  - verified_at null everywhere;
  - every host is covered by routes.json (platforms, out_of_scope or terms_restricted) unless the row is app_only;
  - route_ids exist;
  - every reported or confirmed terms status has a routes.json entry;
  - URLs are http(s);
  - platform-map.md ids and URLs match the JSON.
- korea-statistics.json:
  - source_type is in ergoqa.audience.SOURCE_TYPES;
  - frame fields are present;
  - count_only rows never allow size kinds;
  - aliases are unique.
- markers.json:
  - every string is NFC;
  - no bare words;
  - the promotion-ko fixture passes (positives flagged, negatives not);
  - anonymous_handles includes ㅇㅇ.
- routes.json: terms_restricted and search_pages fields; disabled discovery entries have a reason and sources; new env names use the REMORSEARCH_ prefix.
- agent-tokens.json: tokens match the product-token character set.
- Each korea/*.md has 'Done when' and 'Failure modes', and every path it mentions exists.
- The two copies of the bundle contract are identical.

K1.
- SKILL.md:
  - no BOM; starts with ---;
  - keys are only name and description;
  - name is [a-z0-9-]{1,64}, equals the folder name, and contains neither anthropic nor claude;
  - description is one line of at most 1,024 characters and at most 1,024 bytes, with no ': ', no ' #' and no angle brackets; it is NFC and contains at least 6 requests ending in 해줘.
- agents/openai.yaml has no BOM.
- README.md and README.ko.md:
  - switcher lines present;
  - the same number of ## headings, in the mapped order;
  - the same title.
